      "artist": "M J Richardson",
      "description": "Horsey golf sculpture at Musselburgh One of two new roundabout sculptures installed in November 2009 in Musselburgh, funded by grant aid from East Lothian Council and Awards For All, to promote the sport of horse racing and golf. This one, at the Levenhall Roundabout, celebrates Musselburghs Old Golf Course, the oldest playing golf course in the world. It is by sculptor Ronnie Elliott and is made of 439 horse shoes to combine references to both golf and horse racing, since Musselburgh racecourse, just adjacent, is one of the oldest in Scotland.",
